  "implementation": {
    "storage": "RGBA uses four UInt8 values; no pixel readback or renderer snapshot is supplied.",
    "grammar": "Hex3/4/6/8, twenty explicit base color keywords, comma rgb/rgba with consistent numeric or percent channels and bounded six-digit decimal parts. Other grammar or environment-dependent colors remain explicit.",
    "numeric": "Native binary64 parse/divide/multiply/round order, negative clamps and byte clamps are represented by the logical Float.Model.",
    "cssText": "Accepted keyword identity is retained; numeric values use CSSColorValue rgb/rgba text. The actual byte-alpha two/three-decimal choice is proved equal to the logical Float32 source calculation for all256 bytes in JavaScriptCssColorAlpha.lean.",
    "canvasText": "Opaque colors use lowercase six-digit hex. Alpha uses binary64 byte/255, ECMAScript shortest text and the native Decimal15-digit reduction."
  },
